(418, 1, '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '', 'Python programming', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'python-programming', '', '', '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '2022-01-12 04:37:28', '', 107, 'https://chandani-spacious-ecademy.sites.qsandbox.com/section/python-programming/', 0, 'mto-section', '', 0),
(420, 1, '2022-01-12 04:46:54', '2022-01-12 04:46:54', '<p>In Python, condition statements act depending on whether a given condition is true or false. You can execute different blocks of codes depending on the outcome of a condition. Condition statements always evaluate to either True or False.In control statements, The <code>if</code> statement is the simplest form. It takes a condition and evaluates to either <code>True </code>or <code>False</code>.</p><p style=\"text-align: start\">If the condition is <code>True</code>, then the True block of code will be executed, and if the condition is False, then the block of code is skipped, and The controller moves to the next line.</p>', 'Python Flow Control', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'python-flow-control', '', '', '2026-03-22 21:31:50', '2026-03-23 00:31:50', '', 418, 'https://chandani-spacious-ecademy.sites.qsandbox.com/lesson/python-flow-control/', 0, 'mto-lesson', '', 0),
(422, 1, '2022-01-12 04:49:15', '2022-01-12 04:49:15', '<h2 style=\"text-align: start\">What is a function in Python?</h2><p style=\"text-align: start\">In Python, a function is a group of related statements that performs a specific task.</p><p style=\"text-align: start\">Functions help break our program into smaller and modular chunks. As our program grows larger and larger, functions make it more organized and manageable.</p><p style=\"text-align: start\">Furthermore, it avoids repetition and makes the code reusable.</p><p style=\"text-align: start\">Above shown is a function definition that consists of the following components.</p><ol><li><p>Keyword <code>def</code> that marks the start of the function header.</p></li><li><p>A function name to uniquely identify the function. Function naming follows the same <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.programiz.com/python-programming/keywords-identifier#rules\">rules of writing identifiers in Python</a>.</p></li><li><p>Parameters (arguments) through which we pass values to a function. They are optional.</p></li><li><p>A colon (:) to mark the end of the function header.</p></li><li><p>Optional documentation string (docstring) to describe what the function does.</p></li><li><p>One or more valid python statements that make up the function body. Statements must have the same indentation level (usually 4 spaces).</p></li><li><p>An optional <code>return</code> statement to return a value from the function.</p></li></ol>', 'Python Functions', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'python-functions', '', '', '2026-03-22 21:31:50', '2026-03-23 00:31:50', '', 418, 'https://chandani-spacious-ecademy.sites.qsandbox.com/lesson/python-functions/', 1, 'mto-lesson', '', 0),
(424, 1, '2022-01-12 04:51:42', '2022-01-12 04:51:42', '<p>Now you know <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://realpython.com/interacting-with-python/\">how to interact with the Python interpreter and execute Python code</a>. It’s time to dig into the Python language. First up is a discussion of the basic data types that are built into Python.</p><p><strong>Here’s what you’ll learn in this tutorial:</strong></p><ul><li><p>You’ll learn about several basic <strong>numeric, string</strong>, and <strong>Boolean</strong> types that are built into Python. By the end of this tutorial, you’ll be familiar with what objects of these types look like, and how to represent them.</p></li><li><p>You’ll also get an overview of Python’s built-in <strong>functions.</strong> These are pre-written chunks of code you can call to do useful things. You have already seen <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://realpython.com/courses/python-print/\">the built-in </a><code>print()</code> function, but there are many others.</p></li></ul>', 'Python Datatypes', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'python-datatypes', '', '', '2026-03-22 21:31:50', '2026-03-23 00:31:50', '', 418, 'https://chandani-spacious-ecademy.sites.qsandbox.com/lesson/python-datatypes/', 2, 'mto-lesson', '', 0),
(425, 1, '2022-01-12 04:52:17', '2022-01-12 04:52:17', '', 'Python Control Flow Statements and Loops', '', 'publish', 'open', 'closed', '', 'python-control-flow-statements-and-loops', '', '', '2022-01-12 04:52:17', '2022-01-12 04:52:17', '', 418, 'https://chandani-spacious-ecademy.sites.qsandbox.com/quiz/python-control-flow-statements-and-loops/', 3, 'mto-quiz', '', 0),
